 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Level 3 (inferred): InMemoryDB() starts empty; records hold string fields with string values. Every method takes a timestamp; timestamps across all calls are strictly increasing. setDataAt(key, field, value, timestamp) stores a value that never expires. setDataAtWithTtl(key, field, value, timestamp, ttl) stores a value that is live at times t with timestamp <= t < timestamp + ttl. Setting a field replaces its value and expiry. getDataAt(key, field, timestamp) returns the live value or \"\". deleteDataAt(key, field, timestamp) removes a live field and returns true, otherwise false. scanDataAt(key, timestamp) and scanDataByPrefixAt(key, prefix, timestamp) return the live fields of the record as \"field(value)\" strings ordered by field name, all of them or only those whose field starts with prefix. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk15-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
